claim.claim-text:
a seed housing portion (7A) and a vacant housing portion (7B) releasably attached to each other to form a substantially sealed housing;
a seed disc (5) enclosed in the housing and rotatable in a substantially vertical plane, the seed disc having a seed side (5A) and an opposite vacant side (5B), the seed disc dividing the housing into a seed housing area enclosed by the seed housing portion and a vacant housing area enclosed by the vacant housing portion;
a disc drive (9) operative to rotate the seed disc about a disc rotational axis in a disc rotation direction;
a plurality of seed apertures (11) defined through the seed disc, the seed apertures substantially equally spaced at a substantially equal distance from a rotational axis of the seed disc such that as the seed disc rotates the seed apertures move along a circular seed aperture path;
a circular disc shoulder (55) extends outward from the seed side of the seed disc, the disc shoulder having a shoulder radius less than a path radius of the seed aperture path;
an alignment guide (57) extending laterally outward from a guide location on the disc shoulder;
a seed reservoir (13) formed in a bottom portion of the seed housing area (7A);
a singulator element (59) configured to remove excess seeds from the seed apertures (11) as the seed disc (5) rotates when the singulator element is in a singulator operating position with an inner edge (59B) of the singulator element bearing against an outer face of the disc shoulder (55) and an outer edge (59A) of the singulator element outside the seed aperture path;
an axial bias element (63) mounted to an interior of the seed housing portion and a radial bias element (61) mounted to an interior of the seed housing portion;
wherein the singulating element (59) is attached to the axial bias element (63) such that the axial bias element (63) exerts an axial bias force on the singulator element toward the seed side of the seed disc; and
wherein the radial bias element (61) exerts a radial bias force on the singulator element toward the disc rotational axis;
wherein when the seed disc (5) begins to rotate in the disc rotation direction, the singulator element (59) bears against the alignment guide (57) and the singulator element (59) moves outward along the alignment guide (57) against the radial bias force to the singulator operating position.

mounting the singulator element (59) in the seed housing portion such that the singulator element is movable radially and axially;
mounting an axial bias element (63) in the seed housing portion operative to exert an axial bias force on the singulator element in a direction outward from the seed housing portion;
mounting a radial bias element (61) in the seed housing portion operative to exert a radial bias force on the singulator element toward the disc rotational axis;
providing a circular disc shoulder (55) extending outward from a seed side of the seed disc, the disc shoulder having a shoulder radius less than a path radius of a seed aperture path;
assembling the singulating meter by engaging the seed disc on a driveshaft of the seed housing portion with the disc shoulder facing the singulator element;
rotating the seed disc in the disc rotation direction to exert an outward force on the singulator element against the radial bias force such that the singulator element moves outward against the radial bias force, while the axial bias element exerts the axial bias force on the singulator element toward the seed side of the seed disc, to a singulator operating position where an inner edge (59B) of the singulator element bears against an outer face of the disc shoulder.

a seed housing portion (7A) and a vacant housing portion (7B) releasably attached to each other to form a substantially sealed housing;
a seed disc (5) enclosed in the housing and rotatable in a substantially vertical plane, the seed disc having a seed side (5A) and an opposite vacant side (5B), the seed disc dividing the housing into a seed housing area enclosed by the seed housing portion and a vacant housing area enclosed by the vacant housing portion;
a disc drive (9) operative to rotate the seed disc about a disc rotational axis in a disc rotation direction;
a plurality of seed apertures (11) defined through the seed disc, the seed apertures substantially equally spaced at a substantially equal distance from a rotational axis of the seed disc such that as the seed disc rotates the seed apertures move along a circular seed aperture path;
a seed reservoir (13) formed in a bottom portion of the seed housing area;
a singulator element (59) configured to remove excess seeds from the seed apertures (11) as the seed disc (5) rotates when the singulator element is in a singulator operating position;
an axial bias element (63) mounted to an interior of the seed housing portion and a radial bias element (61) mounted to an interior of the seed housing portion;
wherein the singulating element (59) is magnetically attached to the axial bias element such that the axial bias element exerts (63) an axial bias force on the singulator element toward the seed side of the seed disc; and
wherein the radial bias element (61) exerts a radial bias force on the singulator element toward the disc rotational axis.
